# Python bytecode from the scripts in scripts/.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Brief and specification notes, kept locally and deliberately not published.
# One per tool, sitting beside the module folders, plus a few templates at the
# top of modules/. They were swept into a commit once by a `git add modules`
# and had to be taken back out of history, which is what these two lines exist
# to prevent happening again.
#
# Anchored and single-level on purpose, so that legitimate documentation is
# untouched: teaching-notes.md lives at modules/<module>/tools/<tool>/, the
# five tools/README.md files at modules/<module>/tools/, and neither is three
# levels deep enough to match. docs/*.md, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md,
# LEARNER_COPY_STYLE.md and the root CLAUDE.md are outside modules/ entirely.
/modules/*.md
/modules/*/*.md

# Local-only tooling and editor artefacts. None belongs in a published teaching
# resource. `.Rhistory` was tracked as an empty file until the post-release
# housekeeping pass and had to be removed from the index; the rest are listed
# before rather than after the same mistake.
.claude/settings.local.json
.Rhistory
.Rproj.user/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Oxlint runs from a pinned `npx` invocation and installs nothing, so neither of
# these should ever exist here. They are listed because a maintainer reaching
# for `npm install oxlint` would create both, and the site's promise is that it
# ships no dependencies.
node_modules/
package-lock.json
